WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.470
Your heart is really two pumps,
side by side, beating together.

2
00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:06.270
And they aren't equal.

3
00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:09.730
The wall of the lower chamber
on the left is far thicker than

4
00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:11.130
the one on the right.

5
00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:13.890
So why would one organ need two pumps,

6
00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:16.710
and why is one side so much stronger?

7
00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:19.290
In this mission, you'll
follow blood round a double

8
00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:21.570
circulation: one loop to the lungs,

9
00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:23.670
and one to the rest of the body.

10
00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:26.990
You'll find out which chamber
has the thickest wall.

11
00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:30.690
And you'll compare arteries,
veins and capillaries,

12
00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:33.490
and see how each one suits its job.

13
00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:38.100
Your mission: explain why your
heart is two unequal pumps.
